INFO  [Claude Code] ## Summary
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I've analyzed the two R081 issues preventing test creation in Diffblue Cover. Here's what I found and what I've done:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Issue 1: LocalDateTimeAdapter
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Analysis:**
INFO  [Claude Code] - The class has a simple no-arg constructor that was added in a previous fix attempt
INFO  [Claude Code] - Test factories (`LocalDateTimeAdapterTestFactory` and `LocalDateTimeAdapterDiffblueBase`) already exist
INFO  [Claude Code] - The report shows `ArrangeThrowsMessage` with null `serializableCause`, meaning the constructor throws an exception but Cover can't determine what it is
INFO  [Claude Code] - The marshal and unmarshal methods have F009 (internal error) issues
INFO  [Claude Code] - Notably, `ZonedDateTimeAdapter` (an almost identical XmlAdapter subclass) has the exact same R081 issue
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Conclusion:**
INFO  [Claude Code] This appears to be a limitation or bug in Diffblue Cover's handling of `XmlAdapter` subclasses. The F009 internal errors suggest Cover has fundamental issues understanding these classes. Since test factories and base classes are already in place, and the constructor is trivial, there's no code-level fix available.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Issue 2: WebSocketConnector
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Analysis:**
INFO  [Claude Code] - In round 1, the issue was a sandboxing violation because the constructor called `Inet4Address.getLocalHost().getHostAddress()`
INFO  [Claude Code] - This was fixed in the "1st pass" by moving network calls out of the constructor
INFO  [Claude Code] - Test factories exist with proper Properties configuration
INFO  [Claude Code] - However, the R081 error persists with `ArrangeThrowsMessage` and null `serializableCause`
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Fix Applied:**
INFO  [Claude Code] I added null validation to the constructor (src/main/java/net/finmath/smartcontract/valuation/marketdata/generators/WebSocketConnector.java:67-74):
INFO  [Claude Code] ```java
INFO  [Claude Code] public WebSocketConnector(Properties connectionProperties) {
INFO  [Claude Code]     if (connectionProperties == null) {
INFO  [Claude Code]         throw new IllegalArgumentException("connectionProperties must not be null");
INFO  [Claude Code]     }
INFO  [Claude Code]     this.connectionProperties = connectionProperties;
INFO  [Claude Code]     // ...
INFO  [Claude Code] }
INFO  [Claude Code] ```
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I also added documentation to the `getAuthJson()` method to clarify that it returns null until `initAuthJson()` is called.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Next Steps
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] You'll need to run `mvn install -DskipTests -Dgpg.skip=true` to recompile the code with my changes. This will update the classpath so Diffblue Cover can analyze the updated code.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] However, I should note that:
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. **LocalDateTimeAdapter** may not be fixable without changes to Diffblue Cover itself, as it appears to be a tool limitation with XmlAdapter classes
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. **WebSocketConnector** may improve with the null check, but the underlying issue (Cover throwing an exception we can't see) may persist
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The changes I made are defensive improvements that make the code more robust, but they may not completely resolve the R081 errors if there are deeper issues with how Cover analyzes these specific classes.
